        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "1 & 2 bed apartments in Station View at Hampden Hill are available to view by appointment, contact Savills New Homes on 01 618 1300.\r\n\r\nView our virtual tour here - https://3ddesignbureau.com/360VT/StationView_1Bed/\r\n\r\nBuilt to Passive House standards and achieving an A energy rating, the Station View apartments deliver exceptional energy efficiency throughout the seasons. Designed to use up to 70%* less energy for heating than a standard new build, apartments at Station View help reduce running costs while maintaining consistent warmth, naturally warm walls and comfortable living spaces year-round.\r\n\r\nHampden Hill is a new seaside development located in Donabate Village in North County Dublin. Just 30 minutes from Dublin City Centre, this thoughtfully designed mix of modern, energy-efficient homes is surrounded by natural beauty and heritage. Offering a harmonious blend of coastal tranquillity and easy access to the city, the latest homes to come to market at Hampden Hill include a number of 1 & 2 bedroom apartments which qualify for the Help to Buy scheme and First Home Scheme to help with your deposit and mortgage.\r\n\r\nThe spacious apartments at Station View, Hampden Hill showcase a range of sophisticated contemporary designs, each carefully considered for ease of everyday living. At the heart of every home is a generously proportioned, contemporary kitchen finished with quartz worktops, fully integrated appliances and ceramic hob. The separate utility room provides dedicated space for laundry and additional storage. Living spaces are designed to be both versatile and inviting, combining sleek style with seamless functionality.\r\n\r\nEach home is fully wired for high-speed broadband, with TV, telephone and data points in place. Designed for year-round comfort, each home features an energy-efficient heat pump system and zone-controlled panel radiators. With a BER A2 energy rating, they qualify for green mortgages with lower interest rates.\r\n\r\nHampden Hill also benefits from extensive green space, with a 32-acre nature park forming part of the neighbourhood. With the landscape’s first plantings settling in, this evolving natural setting will feature panoramic viewing points and quiet walking paths, carefully shaped to encourage time outdoors.\r\n\r\nWith the planned reimagining of Smyth’s Bridge House as a key feature and Donabate Village nearby, residents will have easy access to shops, schools, sports clubs and all the essential amenities of a thriving community. Dublin City Centre is within easy reach too, making Hampden Hill an ideal base for those seeking a balance of coastal calm and city convenience. \r\n\r\nThe homes in Hampden Hill are ideal for first-time buyers and growing families alike, offering the perfect balance of space, comfort, and contemporary design within a beautiful coastal setting.\r\n \r\n---\r\n\r\nCGIs for illustrative purposes.\r\n\r\nPlease note, if you submit an enquiry for Station View at Hampden Hill via MyHome.ie, the information you provide will be shared with Cairn for the purposes of responding to your enquiry and providing you with information in respect of the development. Visit www.cairnhomes.com/privacy-policy to view Cairn's privacy statement.\r\n\r\n*A feasibility study was prepared by Mosart for Cairn and is based on information and statistics available at the time of preparation."
      },
